ent-NovaFloraBiolumi = glowing plants
    .desc = Several sticks with bulbous, bioluminescent tips.
ent-NovaFloraBiolumiFlower = glowing flower
    .desc = Beautiful, bioluminescent flower.
ent-NovaFloraBiolumiLamp = plant lamp
    .desc = Bioluminescent plant much in a shape of a street lamp.
ent-NovaFloraBiolumiMine = glowing plant
    .desc = Glowing sphere encased in jungle leaves.
ent-TgFloraAshChilly = springy grassy fruit
    .desc = A number of bright, springy blue fruiting plants. They seem to be unconcerned with the hardy, cold environment.
ent-TgFloraAshDrakeBeet = drake beet
    .desc = An mutated beet. It seems to have adapted to local ecosystems by vaguely mimicking the appearance of a drake. Unsure how that helps, but its probably still tasty.
ent-TgFloraAshFonarstolbe = fonarstolbe fruit
    .desc = A chemotrophic, insignificantly bioluminescent plant dubbed fonarstolbe by spinward scientists. They can survive for weeks in environments and presures lethal to most other plants, as long as they are well rooted..
ent-TgFloraAshGlowgrowth = glowgrowth colony
    .desc = A colony of bioluminescent fungi growing on a hot air vent, feeding off mineral particulate blowing through it.
ent-TgFloraAshInozhakust = inozhakust
    .desc = A plant looking like roots growing into the sky, covered in mushy, wet, oily vines. They squelch and break apart when touched. You'll have to gather them as a paste.
ent-TgFloraLunarPlantStyle1 = lunar plant
    .desc = This seemingly dead plant is actually quite alive, hibernating until sensing living things.
ent-TgFloraLunarPlantStyle2 = lunar plant
    .desc = This seemingly dead plant is actually quite alive, hibernating until sensing living things.
ent-TgFloraLunarPlantStyle3 = lunar plant
    .desc = This seemingly dead plant is actually quite alive, hibernating until sensing living things.
ent-BeeFloraAshStrange = strange plant
    .desc = An alient plant born under warming glow of space radiation. What mysteries does it hold? Botanist should know.
ent-ShiptestAshSpaceVoidmelon = Grown void plant
    .desc = A cluster of strange plants with melonlike fruit attached to their vines.
ent-ShiptestAshGardenArid = rock garden
    .desc = Beneath a bluff of soft silicate, a sheltered grove slumbers.
ent-ShiptestAshGardenFrigid = chilly garden
    .desc = A delicate layer of frost covers hardy brush.
ent-ShiptestAshGardenWaste = sickly garden
    .desc = Polluted water wells up from the cracked earth, feeding a patch of something curious.
ent-ShiptestFloraAshGarden = lush garden
    .desc = In the soil and shade, something softly grows.
ent-AuroraAssunzioneBushLucevine = luce vine cluster
    .desc = The namesake plant for Luceism, the light-centric religion of Assunzione, the Luce Vine is a fruiting vine noted for its astounding resilience to cold following the Dimming. The plant and its bioluminscent fruit, called 'luce bulbs', are considered evidence of miracle to devout Assunzioni.
ent-ShiptestFloraAshFern = cave fern
    .desc = A species of fern with highly fibrous leaves.
ent-CMFloraJunglePlantbot1 = strange tree
    .desc = Some kind of bizarre alien tree. It oozes with a sickly yellow sap.
ent-CMFloraJunglePlanttop1 = strange tree
